{# Frontend review 2026-07-12 C5: map.js execution must wait for the catalog
   globals (catalog-load.js injects it after the fetch resolves), but its
   DOWNLOAD must not sit serialized behind the ~1 MB catalog transfer — the
   preload puts both requests in flight together, so boot() executes map.js
   straight from cache.
   importmap() replaces the hand-written preload since map.js became the entry
   of an ES-module graph. It emits
   both halves of what that graph needs:
     - the <script type="importmap">, which is what makes the rewritten relative
       imports resolvable — AssetMapper rewrites `./i18n.js` to the UNDIGESTED
       public path, and only the importmap maps that to the digested file;
     - the module URLs themselves, digested.
   No entrypoint argument: `map` is a plain importmap entry, so nothing is
   imported here and the catalog gate below is untouched. That also means
   importmap() emits no preload of its own (it only preloads entrypoints), so
   the C5 parallel download stays a hand-written modulepreload — now of a module
   graph, which the browser walks, warming i18n.js/util.js too. #}
{{ importmap([], {nonce: csp_nonce()}) }}
{# Preload the WHOLE module graph, not just the entry: browsers do not walk
   import graphs for modulepreload, so a single map.js preload left the other
   ~25 modules downloading in serial dependency waves after the catalog landed
